{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PV"}],"opens":"The lexicon is one holon listing every lexeme, so a new word writes about 100 KB of text. Pages of a few hundred lexemes would let a new word rewrite one small page. It is an ordinary commit, with no change of format.","restsOn":["Whether anything needs the lexicon read as one list."],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"The lexicon grown by its parts","prev":null}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0GE"}],"opens":"Past about 5,000 commits the latest table is mostly the hashes of small blocks. Folding small blocks together, or checkpointing less often, would keep a cold read near its size today, and changes no name.","restsOn":["The growth measured is simulated, on synthetic writes."],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A table that stays small","prev":null}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0GE"}],"opens":"A client that keeps the last head it trusted can catch a forged store or a rollback from a host, which a client on its first visit cannot.","restsOn":["Where a head is kept, and what a client does when it is told to go back."],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A glass that remembers its head","prev":null}
{"body":{"kept":"In brief, at the author's word: 11 of the 20 utterances, each in the author's own words and at its place in the order, the last without the direction it pasted from another project. Whether each came spoken or typed is the session's own reading. The session's answers were not kept. What it decided stands in the format, src/tools/vectors/README.md, with what is left open at its end. Six agents reasoned about the format and attacked it, at about 684,000 tokens against an estimate of 300,000. Counted names were chosen first and let go when a store could not be taken away, changed and brought back; short unique names cost about 10% more in the whole field, gzipped. GitHub Pages was measured gzipping these files from a throwaway repository, steward-of-cwejman/static-host-test.","on":"2026-11-08","paths":[{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PW"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PX"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PY"}],"said":[{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB04C"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB088"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB098"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0BW"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0DP"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0F2"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0FX"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0GE"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0HX"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0JE"},{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PV"}],"voice":{"$ref":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0Q0"}},"id":"1M6Y8YRYWTTB0PZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000000"],"name":"A fifth session, kept in brief: the store's format settled by attack, the store made blocks, and the code asked for","prev":null}
